  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records strongly establish that hierarchical FCC/B2 architectures, phase load partitioning, plastic deformation of the hard B2 phase, heterogeneous strain hardening, and activation of multiple defect mechanisms can improve strength–ductility synergy in closely related eutectic alloys (especially R1, R4, R6, R7, and R8). Other records establish high-pressure or combined pressure–temperature processing of HEAs through HPT, DAC heating, SPS, and HIP (R3, R11, R14, R18, and R20). However, none applies hexahedron-anvil HPHT treatment to the Al0.7CoCrFeNi lamellar alloy or indicates that it will convert incoherent FCC/B2 lamellae into a coherent hierarchical pattern enabling preferential FCC-to-B2 dislocation transfer. Combining the two literature strands would therefore point in the right direction, but selecting HPHT for this specific interfacial transformation would still require a substantial new idea."
}
